# Trivy ignore list — CONTAINER IMAGE scan only.
#
# Deliberately separate from `.trivyignore`, which governs the filesystem scan
# of this repository's own dependency tree. The two scan different things and
# must not share suppressions: a CVE that is unfixable inside a vendored
# third-party binary is not the same as one in our lockfile, and suppressing it
# in the shared file would switch off the regression detection the filesystem
# gate exists to provide.
#
# CVE-2026-69152 below is the sharp edge that makes the split necessary: it was
# genuinely FIXED in our lockfile (#773), so it must keep failing the
# filesystem scan if it ever regresses — while the copy vendored inside pnpm's
# binary is beyond our reach.
#
# Every entry here needs an `SD-*` row in docs/AUDIT_DEBT.md, same rule as the
# other file. The entry below was labelled `SD-23` by #781, colliding with an
# unrelated resolved row, and had no AUDIT_DEBT row at all; both are fixed now.

# SD-24: three HIGH findings vendored INSIDE the pnpm distribution that ships in
# the backend runtime image. They live in corepack's cached pnpm tree, so
# `pnpm.overrides` cannot reach them and neither can a lockfile change.
#
# pnpm is required at runtime: `scripts/railway-start.js` boots the server with
# `pnpm exec medusa start` and runs migrations with
# `pnpm exec medusa db:migrate --execute-safe-links`. It therefore cannot be
# removed the way npm was — npm IS removed from both node runtime images, and
# that is what cleared most of the image findings.
#
# pnpm was bumped 10.13.1 -> 10.34.5 here, taking the backend image from 51
# HIGH/CRITICAL to 4. The remaining three need pnpm 11.x:
#
#   CVE-2026-69152  brace-expansion 2.1.2  fixed in 2.1.4
#   CVE-2026-69192  ip-address 10.2.0      fixed in 10.3.1
#   CVE-2026-55697  pnpm 10.34.5           fixed in 11.5.3
#
# pnpm 11 clears all three — verified against both corepack caches, the same
# tree this scan reads: 11.20.0 vendors 23 packages against 10.34.5's 80, and
# neither brace-expansion nor ip-address is among them.
#
# It is blocked on Node, not on pnpm. pnpm 11 requires Node >= 22.13 and this
# repo pins Node 20 in CI and in all four Dockerfiles; #787 attempted the bump
# and every job failed with `ERR_UNKNOWN_BUILTIN_MODULE: node:sqlite`. So the
# real prerequisite is a Node 20 -> 22 upgrade of four production runtimes,
# which is its own change rather than a rider on a CVE fix.
#
# SD-24 in docs/AUDIT_DEBT.md carries the full migration plan, including the
# part that makes it dangerous: pnpm 11 silently ignores `pnpm-workspace.yaml`
# overrides when `--ignore-workspace` is passed, which would unpin 84 CVE fixes
# without a single warning. `scripts/check-override-coverage.mjs` now guards
# that and runs before the Trivy filesystem scan.
#
# SD-22: CVE-2026-14257 is a separate finding in OUR OWN tree rather than
# pnpm's bundle, already suppressed in `.trivyignore` for the same unfixable
# function-export line; repeated here because the two files do not share
# entries. It is unaffected by the pnpm upgrade above.
CVE-2026-14257
CVE-2026-69152
CVE-2026-69192
CVE-2026-55697
